pport, demonstrating flexibility, and generating enough interest to secure a follow-up engagement. However, relative to the actual persuasion task (convince Sarah to support the ordinance), the outcome is incomplete. Sarah shows minor belief shifts and openness but stops short of actual support. The persuader's tactical pivot to a lower-commitment request may facilitate future persuasion but does not constitute achievement of the original goal. This represents moderate effectiveness—progress and engagement without full task completion."]
